# Line-ending policy for new and future commits.
#
# This repository's existing files are stored with CRLF. Git does not translate
# them retroactively, and this file deliberately does NOT force `eol=lf` on
# source types: doing so would mark all 144 committed text files for
# renormalisation and produce a whole-repository diff in one commit, burying the
# real V1 changes.
#
# What this file does instead:
#   * keep Git's automatic text/binary detection, so new files are normalised to
#     LF in the object database regardless of the contributor's platform;
#   * mark binaries explicitly, so they can never be line-ending translated or
#     diffed as text;
#   * fix LF for the files this repository actually creates without CRLF, which
#     are not committed here (see the note on lockfiles below).
#
# If a future change wants to move the whole repository to LF, do it as its own
# dedicated commit with `git add --renormalize .`, never mixed into a release.

* text=auto

# ---- binary: never translated, never diffed as text ----
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.webp    binary
*.ico     binary
*.mp4     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ttf     binary
*.eot     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.gz      binary
*.tgz     binary
*.zip     binary
*.wasm    binary

# ---- shell / build tooling: LF, so they stay executable on POSIX ----
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# ---- Windows scripts: CRLF, so cmd/PowerShell run them unmodified ----
*.ps1     text eol=crlf
*.bat     text eol=crlf
*.cmd     text eol=crlf

# ---- lockfile: LF, and never mass-rewritten ----
package-lock.json text eol=lf -diff